0 !ACHILLES {"id":"ACH-Z05-S01","name":"Zone V · Scene 1: Pastoral — Oxen of Gold & Tin and the Two Terrible Lions","zone":"Z05","lines":"18.573–586","greek":"Ἐν δ᾽ ἀγέλην ποίησε βοῶν ὀρθοκραιράων· αἱ δὲ βόες χρυσοῖο τετεύχατο κασσιτέρου τε... σμερδαλέω δὲ λέοντε δύ᾽ ἐν πρώτῃσι βόεσσιν ταῦρον ἐρύγμηλον ἐχέτην· ὁ δὲ μακρὰ μεμυκὼς ἕλκετο· τὸν δὲ κύνες μετεκίαθον ἠδ᾽ αἰζηοί... ἵσταντο δὲ μάλ᾽ ἐγγύς, ὑλάοντές τε καὶ ἐκτὸς ἀλυσκάζοντες.","buckley":"On it he also fashioned a herd of lofty-horned oxen; but the oxen were made of gold and tin; and lowing, they rushed from the stall to the pasture, beside a murmuring river, along the waving reed. Four golden herdsmen accompanied the oxen, and nine dogs, swift of foot, followed them. But two terrible lions among the foremost oxen seized a bellowing bull, and he, dragging, roared loudly; but the dogs and the young men ran up to him. The lions indeed, having torn the hide of the huge ox, were devouring the entrails and the black blood; but the shepherds vainly pressed upon them, urging on the fleet dogs; for they refused to bite the lions, but stood very near, barking, and flying them.","worldModel":{"vision":"Gold (297) and tin (71) horned oxen beside a kyanos river and olive reeds; four golden herdsmen; nine hounds; two tawny lions tearing the bull.","memory":"Repulsion/attraction boundary dynamics: the four herdsmen urge the nine dogs forward, but the dogs stop short of biting, oscillating between lunging to bark (ὑλάοντες) and darting back (ἀλυσκάζοντες).","controller":"Wild nature erupting inside pastoral order — the limit of human and canine control."}}

